From 93035135e393a41b3b6bc6647a92854923c91264 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Myth Claude <claude@ttech.local>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 08:16:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sales): Cash Collected now matches Dashboard; add
 drill-down cards and row Preview/Download

- Cash Collected was summing the filtered list instead of all sales,
  so it silently changed value with the search box / status pill and
  drifted from the Dashboard's Cash Balance whenever a filter was
  active. Now always the sum of every Sale.amount, matching
  build_dashboard_breakdown()'s Cash In exactly (verified live:
  both = MK 41,398,000 against seeded data).
- Stat cards were static; wired up details + onOpenDetails so they
  open DetailBreakdownModal, same pattern as Invoices.jsx/Expenses.jsx.
- Sale rows had no actions at all; added Preview and Download PDF
  buttons that fetch the linked Job (new api.job(id) client method,
  backed by the existing GET /jobs/<id> backend route) and act on
  its embedded invoice, reusing InvoicePrintLayout/downloadInvoicePDF
  rather than inventing a new document type for Sale.

Known gap flagged in code, not fixed here: a Sale row only exists for
a job-linked invoice. Payments on a direct/jobless invoice (still
reachable via routes/invoices.py's apply_payments()) count on the
Dashboard but have no Sale row, so they won't appear here until the
direct invoice payment route is removed per decisions-and-conventions.md.

-- Myth Claude
